kilbil-loyalty-client-proof: the acceptance target. Inline payloads now synthesise, so 34 of 36 operations generate; the two `application/xml` request bodies (`goodsxml`, `goodslistxml`) are what remain. Tracked as xml-content-type-policy.

Two corrections worth recording, because earlier versions of this file got the
same question wrong in opposite directions and both wrong versions informed the
task backlog.

The first version said a `3.1.0` version string would be rejected at a version
gate before anything else could matter. There is no version gate. paogen never
inspects `$openApi->openapi` and never calls `validate()`, so a 3.1 document is
read structurally like any other. That correction stands.

The second version went further and said this document uses no 3.1 construct at
all — "no `type: [T, "null"]`" in as many words. It uses 87 of them: 48
`[string, "null"]`, 26 `[integer, "null"]`, 12 `[array, "null"]`, and one
`[number, "null"]`. Nothing else from 3.1 appears.

So the parser swap is still not what stands between paogen and this client.
`cebe/php-openapi` hands the type list over verbatim while declaring
`Schema::$type` as `string`; it was paogen's reading of it that was wrong, and
`nullable-type-arrays` fixed that without touching the dependency. What is left
is XML request serialisation, and that is the whole of it.
